A1. This would help you to see a long way. ~ TELEVISION
A9. A business man usually overlooks this in the morning. ~ MAIL
A11. A fertilizing clay. ~ MARL
A12. When words fail this is sometimes used to settle the argument. ~ FIST
A15. This is something between England and America that has never been settled. ~ OCEAN
A17. A Christmas carol. ~ NOEL
A19. A little article that writers use. ~ THE
A20. What Mt. Ætna has caused. ~ WOE
A21. This is bad stuff for a clown. ~ SOB
A23. This kind of man is well-groomed. ~ NEAT
A25. The whole crowd. ~ ALL
A27. This is indefinite. ~ AN
A28. This figure that comes after forty. ~ STOUT
A30. A lever worked by the foot. ~ TREADLE
A32. The kind of jokes found in JUDGE. (No raspberries today!) ~ POINTED
A34. This is always found in the hills. ~ DALE
A35. This has fragrant blossoms. ~ LILAC
A37. These are always playing a game of give and take. ~ TRADERS
A39. There are two sides to this. (Abbr.) ~ ST
A40. The way flappers get in. ~ STEP
A41. These stop the flow of liquor. ~ CORKERS
A42. A female Rider Haggard made famous. ~ SHE
A43. This goes in the pot. ~ TEA
A44. This is where the shoe pinches. (Plural) ~ BUNIONS
A45. This is sometimes lost between Chicago and New York. ~ HOUR
A46. Something you'll like at the Statler. (Abbr.) ~ RM
A47. A form that has become obsolete. (Plural) ~ CORSETS
A48. It takes about 30 days to make this. ~ MONTH
A49. This man used to make jokes—his work now isn't as funny as it used to be. ~ FORD
A50. This is a good bunch gone dry. ~ RAISINS
A52. The lid is over this at night. ~ EYEBALL
A55. This should be a rare and juicy one. ~ STEAK
A56. The hand that used to rock the cradle. ~ MA
A57. The only kind of pins the boys use. ~ TEN
A58. What a sore-head should do. ~ HEAL
A60. An affirmative. ~ YES
A61. The kind of debt you'll never collect. ~ BAD
A62. It's dangerous to have this up your sleeve. ~ ACE
A64. What the fast young man did. ~ SPED
A66. What every chorus girl will do before she makes up. ~ SMEAR
A68. This is only half. ~ SEMI
A70. What horizontal 1 will cause things to be. ~ SEEN
A72. Kitty food. ~ ANTE
A73. People who live here need arrest cure. ~ UNDERWORLD

D1. This is the brightest thing about some men. ~ TIE
D2. This is very snappy. ~ ELASTIC
D3. The printer's larger measure. ~ EM
D4. This can move even a hardened criminal. ~ VAN
D5. A good way to remove wrinkles. ~ IRON
D6. It will be a cold day when this comes. ~ SLEET
D7. A preposition. ~ OF
D8. Egg of insect. ~ NIT
D9. When this is full it gets all lit up. ~ MOON
D10. This is a plane man who has a high record. ~ ACE
D13. There is something dark about this. ~ SHADE
D14. What most women do with a secret. ~ TELL
D16. The sandwiching hour. ~ NOON
D18. These should always have plenty of food. ~ LARDERS
D20. This has been rather bullish since the election. ~ WALLSTREET
D22. These should hold under any emergency. ~ BUTTONS
D24. The greatest water-power in the world. ~ TEARS
D26. This is always telling your business. ~ LETTERHEAD
D28. This is good for the soil. ~ SOAP
D29. This leads a dog's life. ~ TERRIER
D31. Whose voice is no longer heard on the raddio? (Poss.) ~ ALS
D32. An entreaty. ~ PLEA
D33. These are both North and South—and pretty far West. ~ DAKOTAS
D36. This is a piece of news. ~ ITEM
D38. Stupidity. ~ DENSITY
D39. The way some people find the door to success. ~ SHUT
D41. Congeals. ~ CURDLES
D42. Little worries of Dad's. ~ SONS
D44. A prominent Senator from the West. ~ BORAH
D45. What any goose will tell you. ~ HONK
D47. A male swan. ~ COB
D48. Pertaining to miasma, malaria. ~ MIASMAL
D49. This runs around a lot. ~ FENCE
D51. What a person does with Horizontal 1. ~ SEES
D53. Affirmative votes. ~ YEAS
D54. What a man has when he forgets his wife's birthday. ~ LAPSE
D56. According to the old song this "ain't what it used to be." ~ MARE
D59. This isn't really good looking. ~ LEER
D61. A sporty club. ~ BAT
D63. Here's that old Australian bird. ~ EMU
D65. This will make the country wet. ~ DEW
D67. This is usually the best part of a pleasure trip. ~ END
D69. The other part of Horizontal 40. ~ IN
D71. A positive negative. ~ NO


